the promise that lessons will be learned  means nothing to parents like these Mia  Harwood was stillborn in Telford three  days after a damning report blamed the  trust there for more than 200 deaths  there'd been an obsession with avoiding  Caesarean sections with a first child  you don't know any different so you  think oh if they're telling me this is  safe then  carry on but every day I was asking if a  C-section was safer they just kept  saying we'll carry on with the induction  and see what happens Mia's heart stopped  while labor was being induced  had Midwife come up to me and ask what  was going to happen I said well you know  she's gone for a post-mortem and then  we'll get some answers and she said  sometimes they don't find anything and  sometimes it's just you  to have your daughter die and then a day  later someone essentially blame you that  was just the worst thing you can say to  anyone  the trust says no individual should ever  be left feeling that they're to blame  but as scandals emerge across the  country there are similar themes parents  not being listened to understaffing and  in some cases an ideology that favors  natural birth Sky News has obtained this  an NHS guide from 2010 to reduce  C-section rates among the benefits it  lists a sense of Pride and financial  savings the Department of Health and  Social care says it doesn't represent  current government policy but three  trusts who helped write it were East  Kent Shrewsbury and Telford and  Nottingham  love hearts for Harriet it was in  Nottingham that lottie's older sister  Harriet was stillborn midwives offered  us aromatherapy when we had an obstetric  emergency they should have called the  Obstetricians to come and do an  emergency Caesarean section  the Nottingham trust says it's truly  sorry Harriet's death is one of more  than 700 cases being investigated there  there are so many different levels of  failures at the minute within the system  I feel like the complete culture needs  to change they fear the consequences if  it doesn't  there will be other parents like us they  just don't know who they are yet  it is the starkist of warnings from a  family who always have one child missing  Becky Johnson Sky News
 

